{
  "web-component/README.md": "# acme icons — Web Component

A framework-free custom element. Works in plain HTML, Vue, Svelte, Lit, Angular (with \`CUSTOM_ELEMENTS_SCHEMA\`) and React.

\`\`\`html
<script type="module" src="./acme-icon.js"></script>
<acme-icon name="home" size="24" color="#0a7d3b" label="home"></acme-icon>
\`\`\`

Attributes: \`name\`, \`size\` (number = px or any CSS length), \`color\`, \`stroke-width\`, \`label\` (omit for decorative icons).
CSS variables also work and cross the shadow boundary: \`--acme-icon-size\`, \`--acme-icon-color\`, \`--acme-icon-color-2…\`, \`--acme-icon-stroke-width\`.

The file contains every icon (3). Need fewer? Delete entries from \`ACME_ICONS\`, or import from \`react/\` / \`angular/\` for per-icon imports.
Typings: \`acme-icon.d.ts\`.
",
